{"kind":"finding","id":"F-ledger-career-030-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/KerbalLoadDiagnosticsTests.cs","line":344,"method":"ApplyToRoster_FacadePath_WithFailedHistoricalRecreate_DoesNotLogFalseKeep","category":"T1","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/KerbalsModule.cs:1819; deleting the TryGetStatus continue -> stays green because no diagnostic event exists to fire; asserting KerbalLoadRepairDiagnostics.CurrentForTesting counters are 0 after ApplyToRoster -> red on any false keep/recreate record","what_it_asserts":"A failed historical stand-in recreate records nothing that would emit a repair summary, and Kirrim stays out of the fake roster.","why_weak":"The fake roster never contains Kirrim, so the step-3 record loop at KerbalsModule.cs:1815-1825 skips before it can call RecordRetiredStandInRecreated/Kept; the summary gate is never reached with a Kept count (and RetiredStandInsKept alone is not an interesting change). The Contains(Kirrim) false is the fake's configured TryRecreateStandIn refusal, not a recorded production outcome.","proposed_action":"Assert KerbalLoadRepairDiagnostics.CurrentForTesting.RetiredStandInsRecreated == 0 (and Kept == 0) directly after ApplyToRoster, so a false-recreate record reds; keep EmitAndReset only for the summary-line assertion.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
